{
  "name": "composer-configuration",
  "version": "3.261121.0",
  "source": "FiligranHQ/xtm-composer@832c5b1 (config/default.yaml, src/config/settings.rs, src/orchestrator/podman/mod.rs)",
  "intro": "The 100 settings XTM Composer 3.261121.0 reads, block by block: its own (`manager`), the connection to each platform and the container engine it deploys the integrations on. Each key is also an environment variable: the key in upper case, with `__` between its levels. [Configure XTM Composer](/deploy/integrations/configure-composer/) explains how to set them.",
  "filter": "Filter settings and variables",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Manager",
      "columns": [
        "Setting",
        "Environment variable",
        "Type",
        "Default",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.credentials_key_filepath",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.credentials_key_filepath`",
            "`MANAGER__CREDENTIALS_KEY_FILEPATH`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "Path of the file holding the RSA private key; takes priority over `manager.credentials_key` when both are set."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.credentials_key",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.credentials_key`",
            "`MANAGER__CREDENTIALS_KEY`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "RSA private key (PEM, 4096 bits) that decrypts the connectors' secret settings the platform sends; set it, or `manager.credentials_key_filepath`, from a secret."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.debug.show_env_vars",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.debug.show_env_vars`",
            "`MANAGER__DEBUG__SHOW_ENV_VARS`",
            "Boolean",
            "`false`",
            "Whether Composer logs the environment variables of each connector it deploys, with the secret values masked, to check what a connector receives."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.debug.show_sensitive_env_vars",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.debug.show_sensitive_env_vars`",
            "`MANAGER__DEBUG__SHOW_SENSITIVE_ENV_VARS`",
            "Boolean",
            "`false`",
            "With `manager.debug.show_env_vars`, whether the logs show the secret values too; only for a short investigation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.execute_schedule",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.execute_schedule`",
            "`MANAGER__EXECUTE_SCHEDULE`",
            "Integer",
            "`10`",
            "Seconds between two passes of Composer over the connectors (deploy, start, stop, update to match the platform); also the wait between two attempts to reach Docker or Podman at start."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.id",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.id`",
            "`MANAGER__ID`",
            "String",
            "`default-manager-id`",
            "Unique identifier of this XTM Composer: the platform lists it under this id and assigns it the connectors it manages. Give each Composer its own id."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.image_tag_suffix",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.image_tag_suffix`",
            "`MANAGER__IMAGE_TAG_SUFFIX`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "Suffix Composer adds to the tag of every connector image it deploys, `-fips` or `-ubi9`, for the FIPS or Red Hat UBI builds of the connectors (`6.9.0` becomes `6.9.0-fips`, an image without a tag `latest-fips`). Any other value stops Composer at start. The FIPS image of Composer sets `-fips`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.logger.console",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.logger.console`",
            "`MANAGER__LOGGER__CONSOLE`",
            "Boolean",
            "`true`",
            "In this version, turns on the daily log files of the `logs` folder next to the binary (the code swaps it with `manager.logger.directory`)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.logger.directory",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.logger.directory`",
            "`MANAGER__LOGGER__DIRECTORY`",
            "Boolean",
            "`true`",
            "In this version, turns on the logs on the standard output (the code swaps it with `manager.logger.console`)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.logger.format",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.logger.format`",
            "`MANAGER__LOGGER__FORMAT`",
            "String",
            "`json`",
            "Format of the logs on the standard output: `json` or `pretty`; the log files are always JSON."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.logger.level",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.logger.level`",
            "`MANAGER__LOGGER__LEVEL`",
            "String",
            "`info`",
            "Level of Composer's logs: `trace`, `debug`, `info`, `warn` or `error`."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.name",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.name`",
            "`MANAGER__NAME`",
            "String",
            "`Filigran connector manager`",
            "Name the platform shows for this XTM Composer."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:manager.ping_alive_schedule",
          "cells": [
            "`manager.ping_alive_schedule`",
            "`MANAGER__PING_ALIVE_SCHEDULE`",
            "Integer",
            "`60`",
            "Seconds between two signals of life Composer sends to the platform."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "text": "XTM Composer reads `config/default.yaml`, then `config/<COMPOSER_ENV>.yaml` (or `.toml`; `COMPOSER_ENV` is `production` when unset) when it exists, then the environment: a variable is the key in upper case with `__` between levels. The `openaev` block takes the same keys as the `opencti` block below (variables `OPENAEV__...`)."
    },
    {
      "title": "OpenCTI connection",
      "columns": [
        "Setting",
        "Environment variable",
        "Type",
        "Default",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.connect_timeout",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.connect_timeout`",
            "`OPENCTI__CONNECT_TIMEOUT`",
            "Integer",
            "`10`",
            "Seconds Composer waits to open a connection to the platform."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.enable",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.enable`",
            "`OPENCTI__ENABLE`",
            "Boolean",
            "`true`",
            "Whether Composer manages the connectors of an OpenCTI platform."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.http_proxy",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.http_proxy`",
            "`OPENCTI__HTTP_PROXY`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "HTTP proxy URL, with `opencti.with_proxy`; unset, Composer takes `HTTP_PROXY` from its environment."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.https_proxy_ca",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.https_proxy_ca`",
            "`OPENCTI__HTTPS_PROXY_CA`",
            "List of strings",
            "Not set",
            "CA certificates of an intercepting proxy, each a file path or an inline PEM: Composer mounts them in each connector and points `SSL_CERT_FILE`, `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`, `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS` and `CURL_CA_BUNDLE` to them."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.https_proxy_reject_unauthorized",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.https_proxy_reject_unauthorized`",
            "`OPENCTI__HTTPS_PROXY_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED`",
            "Boolean",
            "`true`",
            "Whether the connectors reject a proxy certificate they cannot verify; `false` passes `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` to them."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.https_proxy",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.https_proxy`",
            "`OPENCTI__HTTPS_PROXY`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "HTTPS proxy URL, with `opencti.with_proxy`; unset, Composer takes `HTTPS_PROXY` from its environment."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.logs_schedule",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.logs_schedule`",
            "`OPENCTI__LOGS_SCHEDULE`",
            "Integer",
            "`10`",
            "Seconds between two reports of the connectors' logs to the platform, at most."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.no_proxy",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.no_proxy`",
            "`OPENCTI__NO_PROXY`",
            "String",
            "Not set",
            "Hosts reached without the proxy, comma-separated, passed to the connectors; unset, Composer takes `NO_PROXY` from its environment."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.request_timeout",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.request_timeout`",
            "`OPENCTI__REQUEST_TIMEOUT`",
            "Integer",
            "`30`",
            "Seconds Composer waits for an answer of the platform API."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.token",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.token`",
            "`OPENCTI__TOKEN`",
            "String",
            "`ChangeMe`",
            "API token of the user Composer authenticates with on the platform."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.unsecured_certificate",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.unsecured_certificate`",
            "`OPENCTI__UNSECURED_CERTIFICATE`",
            "Boolean",
            "`false`",
            "Whether Composer accepts a platform TLS certificate it cannot verify; only for a test platform."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.url",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.url`",
            "`OPENCTI__URL`",
            "String",
            "`http://host.docker.internal:4000`",
            "URL of the OpenCTI platform, as Composer reaches it."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "composer:opencti.with_proxy",
          "cells": [
            "`opencti.with_proxy`",
            "`OPENCTI__WITH_PROXY`",
            "Boolean",
            "`false`",
            "Whether Composer goes through a proxy to reach the platform and passes the proxy settings (`HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY`, `NO_PROXY` and the CA) to the connectors it deploys; off, it ignores every proxy, even the system's."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
